---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles affiliate links, advertising and sponsored content.`}
  lede="How commercial relationships are shown on this site."
  updated="October 13, 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is free to read. Some pages include product links that may earn a commission.
    Advertising may also appear if it is enabled. Commercial relationships should be identified
    where they affect a recommendation.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some product links may be affiliate links. If you buy through one, {SITE.name} may receive
    a commission from the retailer. The retailer sets the price and terms. Articles containing
    affiliate links display a notice near the article content.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some articles link to Amazon products. A product link does not mean that we bought, tested,
    or photographed the item. Check its current specifications, price, and return terms with the
    retailer before purchase.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is enabled only when the site is configured for advertising and consent
    management. If enabled, Google selects the individual ads; their appearance is not an
    endorsement. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for information about
    advertising technologies and consent.
  </p>
  <h2>Sponsored content and gifted items</h2>
  <p>
    If a page contains paid placement or a gifted product, that relationship should be identified
    on the page. Contact us if you see a relationship that appears to be missing.
  </p>

  <h2>Photography</h2>
  <p>
    Article images include illustrative stock photography from third-party image services, including
    Unsplash and Pexels. Individual photographer and source links appear with some images. Images
    should not be read as documentation of a project tested or photographed by Small Cozy Home.
    Product images may be owned by the relevant retailer.
  </p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If anything here is unclear, or you think we have got a disclosure wrong, tell us at
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We would rather fix it.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
